{"id":"a7d38e47660167fe","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-markov-chain.md","title":"Markov Chain","display":"df-markov-chain — Markov Chain","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-markov-chain","aliases":["58-df-markov-chain","Markov Chain"],"display":"df-markov-chain — Markov Chain","depends_on":["[[../batch05/58-df-stochastic-process.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-markov-chain"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-markov-chain</span><span>Markov Chain</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-markov-chain — Markov Chain"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" href=\"?note=b5f77bed7dfe3f07\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-stochastic-process.md\">../batch05/58-df-stochastic-process.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a7eff3413ce92299\" href=\"?note=a7eff3413ce92299\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md\">../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,S,P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V\">\\(X,S,P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\(\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (transition-matrix predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a7eff3413ce92299\" href=\"?note=a7eff3413ce92299\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md\">../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S\\subseteq V^6\\cup V\">\\(\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S\\subseteq V^6\\cup V\\)</span> (precise predicate and compatibility projection defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall s\\in S^{n+2}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)&gt;0\\to\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n+1\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad=P(\\langle s(n),s(n+1)\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain}\\vdash{}&amp;\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall s\\in S^{n+2}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)&gt;0\\to\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n+1\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad=P(\\langle s(n),s(n+1)\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P\\in V\\;\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P\\in V\\;\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The precise predicate retains the probability space, state set, and transition matrix, and states the conditional law against every finite positive-probability history.</li>\n<li>Markov: the next-state law depends on the current state rather than the earlier history.</li>\n<li>Transition matrix: rows sum to 1</li>\n<li>Multi-step transition: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(P^m)_{ij}=\\mathbb{P}(X_{n+m}=j\\mid X_n=i)\">\\((P^m)_{ij}=\\mathbb{P}(X_{n+m}=j\\mid X_n=i)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>A stationary distribution satisfies <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi P=\\pi\">\\(\\pi P=\\pi\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sum_i\\pi_i=1\">\\(\\sum_i\\pi_i=1\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For a finite irreducible aperiodic chain, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P^n\">\\(P^n\\)</span> converges to a matrix whose rows equal the unique stationary distribution.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Norris, Markov Chains</li>\n<li>Meyn and Tweedie, Markov Chains and Stochastic Stability</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch05/58-df-stochastic-process.md","status":"resolved","id":"b5f77bed7dfe3f07","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-stochastic-process.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md","status":"resolved","id":"a7eff3413ce92299","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md","status":"resolved","id":"a7eff3413ce92299","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ (transition-matrix predicate, see [[../batch08/58-df-transition-matrix.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,S,P,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S\\subseteq V^6\\cup V","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain}\\vdash{}&\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{TransitionMatrix}_S(P,X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall s\\in S^{n+2}\\;\\Bigl(\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)>0\\to\\\\\n&\\qquad\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n+1\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\qquad=P(\\langle s(n),s(n+1)\\rangle)\\,\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\{\\xi\\in\\Omega:\\forall k\\leq n\\;(X(\\langle k,\\xi\\rangle)=s(k))\\}\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}markov\\text{-}chain\\text{-}compatibility}\\vdash\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P\\in V\\;\\mathrm{MarkovChain}_S(X,S,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,P)","display":true},{"tex":"(P^m)_{ij}=\\mathbb{P}(X_{n+m}=j\\mid X_n=i)","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi P=\\pi","display":false},{"tex":"\\sum_i\\pi_i=1","display":false},{"tex":"P^n","display":false}],"bytes":2177,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-817","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-markov-chain.md|58-df-markov-chain]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["b5f77bed7dfe3f07","a7eff3413ce92299"]}